 # Network persona captures
 
+## Production support matrix
+
+| Template | Chrome build | Platform | Feature state | Golden evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 149001 | 149.0.7827.114 | macOS arm64 | `TlsMldsaSignatures=off` | Raw ClientHello body, parsed TLS fields, exact H2 first write |
+| 149002 | 149.0.7827.114 | macOS arm64 | `TlsMldsaSignatures=on` | Raw ClientHello body, parsed TLS fields, exact H2 first write |
+
+Both network variants belong to complete identity template `149000`. That is
+currently the only production complete identity, so complete identity rotation
+is unavailable until a second independently captured, correlated identity is
+added. Chrome 147-148 and Windows/Linux have no production template in this
+catalog. Tests that reject those versions are compatibility guards, not hidden
+fallback templates.
+
+## Capture and verification
+
 These fixtures are raw TLS ClientHello handshake bodies captured from the
 Chromium 149.0.7827.114 macOS arm64 production SSLClientSocket path. The test
 profile used a 32-byte 0x42 Persona seed and generation 7 for the default
 variant, and generation 8 with the existing Chromium ML-DSA signature feature
 set for the ML-DSA variant.
 
+The capture workflow runs that SSLClientSocket path against Chromium's embedded
+BoringSSL test server. The server's `client_hello_callback_for_testing` parses
+the emitted cipher suites, extension order, supported groups, key shares,
+signature algorithms, supported versions, and ALPN. The raw outbound
+ClientHello handshake body is stored in the matching `.hex` fixture and its
+SHA-256 is pinned in the template catalog. The regression test recreates the
+same feature state, seed, and generation and compares parsed protocol fields;
+the fixture hash separately protects the original bytes.
+
 The random, session ID, key-share material, and GREASE values are preserved as
 captured. Regression tests parse protocol fields and normalize GREASE before
 comparison; they do not require cryptographic random bytes to repeat.
