+There is not yet an independent raw HTTP/2 HEADERS fixture or a decrypted
+QUIC/HTTP/3 golden capture. H2 SETTINGS order, connection WINDOW_UPDATE, and
+pseudo-header order are asserted against exact serializer output. H3 SETTINGS
+and reproducible QUIC transport parameters are asserted through the production
+serializers. Future raw fixtures must be captured from an authentic build and
+must not be reconstructed from the expected catalog values.
+
 Persona mode derives separate connection-scoped seeds for TLS extension order,
 HTTP/3 GREASE, and QUIC transport parameter ordering. These seeds never replace
 Chromium's cryptographic randomness for connection IDs, key shares, session
 tokens, or TLS key material.
+
+## Adding a template
+
+Record the exact Chromium full version, operating system and architecture,
+feature state, Persona seed/generation used for capture, capture path, and all
+available raw fixtures. A complete identity must correlate UA, UA-CH, platform,
+TLS, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 behavior from the same browser identity. Do not assemble
+JA3/JA4 or protocol fields by hand, and do not add combinations that the
+current Chromium, BoringSSL, or QUIC stack cannot emit.
